          "line": 66,
          "text": "    When an ephemeral key is compromised, a new signing key pair is created,"
        },
        {
          "line": 67,
          "text": "    along with a new manifest vouching for it (with a higher sequence number),"
        },
        {
          "line": 68,
          "text": "    signed by the master key.  When a rippled peer receives the new manifest,"
        },
        {
          "line": 69,
          "text": "    it verifies it with the master key and (assuming it's valid) discards the"
        },
        {
          "line": 70,
          "text": "    old ephemeral key and stores the new one.  If the master key itself gets"
        },
        {
          "line": 71,
          "text": "    compromised, a manifest with sequence number 0xFFFFFFFF will supersede a"
        },
        {
          "line": 72,
          "text": "    prior manifest and discard any existing ephemeral key without storing a"
        },
        {
          "line": 73,
          "text": "    new one.  These revocation manifests are loaded from the"
